                <pb facs="0375" n="282" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg282"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.51B861/101: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-07-30T16:00:00-04:00">July 30, 1935—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>158. Referring to Department’s telegram No. 109, July 24, 6 p.m., local
                    representative of Bemberg and Company, who are intermediaries in loan matter,
                    advises the Embassy that he understands that complaint of discrimination by the
                    Foreign Bondholders Protective Council has been withdrawn and that negotiations
                    are continuing directly between the interested parties. Please reply by
                    telegraph if further action is desired.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
